userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: The cross-ratio of four collinear points is preserved under projection from any center, so three point-sets that are projections of one another (P, Q, R) share one invariant value even when one point lies at infinity.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Because the cross-ratio of four collinear points is unchanged by projection from any center, a value measured on an image line equals the value on the original 3D line — a projective invariant that survives even a point at infinity.
DEMO STEPS: 4 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

